      *SYSTEM NAME:   EDITORIAL SYSTEMS
      *APPL NAME:     OEM PARTS UPDATE
      *PROGRAM NAME:  MPTZ026 - PRICE UPDATE PROGRAM
      *LANGUAGE:      COBOL II / ORACLE
      *DESCRIPTION:
      *  FUNCTION: THIS PGM SEQUENTIALLY UPDATES THE PARTS DATABASE
      *            BY EITHER DISCONTINUING OLD PARTS ASSOCIATED TO
      *            LINES, DELETING OLD PARTS NOT ASSOCIATED TO LINES,
      *            UPDATING PARTS WITH NEW PRICES, OR INSERTING NEW
      *            PARTS.
      *
      *  INPUT:    CONTROL INFORMATION (PROGRAM PARM FILE)
      *            REFORMATTED TRANSACTION FILE
      *            ORACLE CEG LINE TABLE
      *            ORACLE WIP LINE TABLE
      *            ORACLE CEG SERVICE TABLE
      *
      *  I/O:      ORACLE OEM TABLE
      *            ORACLE PARTS TABLES
      *            ORACLE ALTERNATE PARTS TABLE
      *            ORACLE RESTART TABLE
      *            ORACLE REPORT TABLE
      *
      *  OUTPUT:   DATABASE UPDATE CONTROL REPORT
      *
      *
      * SIGNIFICANT PROCESSING NARRATIVE:
      *  FUNCTION: THIS PGM SEQUENTIALLY UPDATES THE PARTS DATABASE.
      *            THERE ARE FOUR TYPES OF DATABASE UPDATES PERFORMED:
      *            1) PRICE UPDATES (FOR PARTS THAT HAVE A PRICE UPDATE
      *               TRANSACTION SUPPLIED BY THE OEM).
      *            2) NEW PART AND PRICE ADDED (WHEN A PRICE UPDATE
      *               TRANSACTION WAS SUPPLIED FOR A PART NOT ON THE
      *               DATABASE -AND- NOT SUPERSEDED).
      *            3) PART DISCONTINUED (IF NO PRICE UPDATE SUPPLIED,
      *               THE OEM DOESN'T SUPPLY DISCONTINUE TRANSACTIONS,
      *               AND THE PART HASN'T BEEN PRICED WITHIN A SPECIFIC
      *               TIME PERIOD AS DEFINED IN THE BUSINESS RULES).
      *            4) PART DELETED (IF NO PRICE UPDATE SUPPLIED, PART
      *               IS NOT ASSOCIATED TO ANY LINES) AND MEETS OTHER
      *               CRITERIA AS STATED IN THE BUSINESS RULES). IF
      *               THERE ARE ALT PARTS ATTACHED TO THE DELETED PART,
      *               THEY MUST BE DELETED AS WELL.
      *
      *            PARTS WHOSE PRICES HAVE INCREASED MORE THAN 25% ARE
      *            WRITTEN TO A ORACLE TABLE FOR LATER UPDATE REPORTING.
      *
      *            ALSO, ERRONEOUS TRANSACTIONS ARE WRITTEN TO A ORACLE
      *            TABLE FOR LATER REPORTING. PRICE UPDATES FOR SUPER-
      *            SEDED PARTS ARE TALLIED AND NOTED IN THE CONTROL RPT.
      *
      *  NOTE:     THIS PROGRAM CAN ALSO BE RUN IN REPLAEMENT MODE BY
      *            SETTING THE APPROPRIATE PARM. IN THIS SITUATION, THE
      *            UPDATE OF PRICES INVOLVES A DIRECT OVERLAY OF THE
      *            CURRENT PRICE WITH THE NEW PRICE (WITH NO SHIFT OF
      *            THE CURRENT PRICE TO PREVIOUS). DELETES, CALCULATED
      *            DISCONTINUES, & NEW PARTS ARE HANDLED AS USUAL.
      *
      *
      * CALLED PROGRAMS:
      *            ilboabno - abend routine
      *    CALL "dberrmsg" USING SQLCA ERROR-MESSAGE ERROR-LENGTH.
      *
      * CONTROL CARD:
      *  (SAME CONTROL CARD THAT'S USED IN THE UPDATE PROGRAMS)
      *
      *  OEM=XXX,REGN=XX,EFFDT=XX/XX/XXXX,REPLACE=X,RUNTYP=XXX,
      *       1        2           3              4         5
      *
      *  NAGSTYP=XXXXXXXX
      *              6
      *
      *       1 - NUMERIC; OEM NUMBER WHICH YOU ARE PROCESSING
      *
      *       2 - ALPHA; REGION OF THE OEM
      *
      *       3 - NUMERIC; PRICE EFFECTIVE DATE AS SPECIFIED BY THE
      *           OEM (FORMAT MM/DD/YYYY;MUST BE GREATER THAN LAST RUN
      *           UNLESS THIS IS REPLACEMENT RUN-THEN MUST = LAST RUN)
      *
      *       4 - ALPHA; REPLACEMENT INDICATOR (FOR PRICE UPDATE PGM);
      *           (N = NEW RUN, PRICES WILL BE UPDATED - CURRENT MOVED
      *           TO PREVIOUS THEN TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED TO CURRENT;
      *           Y = REPLACEMENT RUN, TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED DIRECTLY
      *           OVER CURRENT PRICE; USED FOR CORRECTING MISPRICING.)
      *
      *       5 - ALPHA; TYPE OF RUN (OEM = OEM, SUP = SUPPLIMENTAL)
      *           (USED BY REPORT PROGRAM MPTZ007)
      *
      *       6 - ALPHA; TYPE OF NAGS RUN (FOR NAGS RUN, EITHER "IMPORT"
      *           OR "DOMESTIC"; ANY OTHER RUNS, "N/A")
      *           (PRINTED IN HEADING - JUST TO DISTINGUISH BETWEEN THE
      *            IMPORT AND DOMESTIC RUN REPORTS)
      *
