      *     3. IF PART WAS PREVIOUSLY PRICED, CHECK IF PRICES ARE   *
      *        THE SAME OR NOT OR IF THIS IS REPLACEMENT RUN.       *
      *        A) IF NOT REPLACEMENT RUN,                           *
      *            - NEW PRICE, MOVE CURRENT INFO TO PREV. INFO.    *
      *                         CALCULATE AND CHECK PRICE VARIANCE, *
      *                         MOVE TRANS PRICE TO CURRENT INFO.   *
      *            - SAME PRICE, SKIP CHANGES TO CURR/PREV INFO     *
      *        B) IF REPLACEMENT RUN, OVERLAY CURRENT PRICE WITH    *
      *                               TRANS PRICE (& CALCULATE      *
      *                               VARIANCE IF OVERLAYING PRICE  *
      *                               DIFFERENT THAN PREV PRICE.)   *
      *     4. UPDATE LAST PRICED DATE AND NULL OUT DISC DATE.      *
      *     5. UPDATE PART ROW                                      *
      *     6. GET NEXT ORACLE ROW                                  *
      *     7. GET NEXT TRANS RECORD                                *
      ***************************************************************
       C2000-DB-EQ-TRANS.
           MOVE "C2000-DB-EQ-TRANS.       " TO WS-PARAGRAPH.

           ADD 1 TO RS-PROC-CTR.

           PERFORM D1000-GET-COUNTS THRU D1000-EXIT.

      * IF PART IS NOT PRICED
           IF WS-NULLIND-PDT NOT EQUAL ZERO
             PERFORM D4000-BUILD-CURR-PRICE   THRU D4000-EXIT
             PERFORM C2200-ADDTO-PRUPCHI-CTRS THRU C2200-EXIT
             IF REPLACEMENT-RUN
               PERFORM C2300-ADDTO-REPL-PRUPCHI-CTRS THRU C2300-EXIT
               GO TO C2000-CONTINUE
             ELSE
               GO TO C2000-CONTINUE.

      * DETERMINE IF REGULAR OR REPLACEMENT RUN.

           IF REPLACEMENT-RUN
             GO TO C2000-REPLACEMENT.

       C2000-REGULAR.
           MOVE "C2000-REGULAR.           " TO WS-PARAGRAPH.

      * WILL PRICE CHANGE AS A RESULT OF THIS TRANSACTION

           IF WS-TR-PRICE EQUAL WS-CURR-PRICE-AMT
             PERFORM C2400-ADDTO-PRUPSAM-CTRS THRU C2400-EXIT
           ELSE
             PERFORM D3000-MOVE-CURR-PREV     THRU D3000-EXIT
             PERFORM D4000-BUILD-CURR-PRICE   THRU D4000-EXIT
             PERFORM C2100-PRICE-VARIANCE     THRU C2100-EXIT
             IF WS-TR-PRICE > WS-PREV-PRICE-AMT
               PERFORM C2200-ADDTO-PRUPCHI-CTRS THRU C2200-EXIT
             ELSE
               PERFORM C2250-ADDTO-PRUPCHD-CTRS THRU C2250-EXIT.

           GO TO C2000-CONTINUE.

       C2000-REPLACEMENT.
           MOVE "C2000-REPLACEMENT.       " TO WS-PARAGRAPH.

      * REMOVED CURR-TO-PREV PRICE IMPACT  ISR:03/16/99)
      * FIRST:
      *    IF THE TAPE PRICE AND PREVIOUS PRICE ARE EQUAL DON'T CALCULATE
      *    A PRICE VARIANCE, BECAUSE THE OEM IS SAYING THE PRICE CHANGE
      *    IN THE ORIGINAL RUN SHOULD NOT HAVE TAKEN PLACE.
      *    SO JUST ADD TO THE PRICE-UPDATE-SAME COUNTER.
      * SECOND:
      *    WHEN THE CURRENT PRICE AND THE TRANS PRICE ARE EQUAL AND
      *    IF THE CURRENT EFFECTIVE DATE DOESN'T = THE TRANSACTION DATE
      *    THEN THE PRICE WAS THE SAME ON THE ORIGINAL RUN AND DID NOT
      *    CHANGE, THIS MEANS THE PRICE WAS SET AT LEAST 2 RUNS AGO.
      *    REMEMBER - THE REPLACEMENT RUN DATE HAS TO BE SET TO THE
      *    ORIGINAL RUN DATE IN THE PARM BEFORE THE REPLACEMENT RUN!!!
      *    SO BYPASS THE VARIANCE CALCULATION.
      * THIRD:
      *   PERFORM THE PRICE VARIANCE PROCEDURE
      *   AND IF THE PRICE HAS CHANGED,ADD TO THE PRICE-UPDATE-COUNTERS
      *   INSTEAD OF THE REPLACEMENT-COUNTERS BECAUSE THE REPLACEMENT RUN
      *   ACTUALLY REFECTS A NEW (UPDATED) PRICE & WE NEED TO COUNT THEM

           IF WS-TR-PRICE EQUAL WS-PREV-PRICE-AMT
             PERFORM C2400-ADDTO-PRUPSAM-CTRS THRU C2400-EXIT
           ELSE
             IF  WS-TR-PRICE = WS-CURR-PRICE-AMT
             AND WS-CURR-EFF-DT NOT = CNTL-EFF-DT
                NEXT SENTENCE
